# Cursor Usage

## Plan first

- Complex work: divide scope + owners in `[Simon]` briefing before implementation.
- User asks "plan only": no code mods; present plan only.
- Large changes needing spec: leave research/plan docs in `documents/` first.
- Min order before implementation: research doc → plan MD → human approval → implementation. See canonical 10-stage pipeline in [protocols/README.md](mdc:protocols/README.md).

## @ References

- Check character roles in `@persona/README.md` + each card.
- UI work: also read `@persona/gina-gui.md`.
- Architecture decisions: prioritize `@.cursor/rules/architecture.mdc`.

## Memo

- Reflect recurring mistakes, project decisions, next tasks in `documents/CURSOR_MEMO.md` when user requests.
- When updating memo, leave date + short reason.

## Multiple chats

- Maintain layer boundaries even when conversations split by area.
- Applying conclusions from another chat: re-verify against files.

## Bugbot

- Follow [bugbot-policy.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/bugbot-policy.mdc): not every PR — only high-risk, large diff, user asks, or similar; no default checklist item.

## Completion report

- Briefly report changed files, validation commands, reasons for anything not run.
- Validation fails: note failing command, reason, next responsible character.
- Validation not run: note commands not executed, reason, remaining risk.
- If `black .` changes files, note format changes separately from pass/fail.
